  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></msub><mn>1</mn></math> reaction rate depends upon the stability of the carbocation, as carbocation formation is the rate determining step compound (ii), forms at <math><mn>2</mn><mo>°</mo></math> allylic carbocation which is the most stable, the next stable carbocation is formed from (iii), it is a <math><mn>2</mn><mo>°</mo></math> carbocation, (i) forms the least stable <math><mn>1</mn><mo>°</mo></math> carbocation, the order of reactivity is thus, <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/26b67605-3ce3-4074-a414-14450fb862d7.jpeg\" style=\"width:4.78333in;height:0.95833in\">",
